==== Opening the case ====

**Note:** This will void your warranty!

Remove Phillips screws on bottom of case.
Gently pry top from base. Use a putty knife inserted between the top and bottom and gentle pressure to release the plastic catches. The ones near the ethernet ports at the back of the unit seem to release the easiest, so start there and work around the perimeter. This takes some patience, but can be done without damage to the case.

Reassembly: press top and bottom together until snaps. Replace screws in bottom of unit.

